<title>GERMANY: Alcatel SEL says to cut 1,500 jobs.</title>
<headline>Alcatel SEL says to cut 1,500 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcatel SEL AG said on Tuesday it planned to cut 1,500 jobs in 1997, after cutting the same number last year, in an effort to return to profitability this year.</p>
<p>The German telecommunications unit of France's Alcatel Alsthom said the layoffs were absolutely necessary to get back in the black.</p>
<p>The company's works council put the number of planned job cuts at 2,100 in 1997, one in every six workers.</p>
<p>The accelerated digitalisation of Germany's telephone network, now nearly completed, has made redundant many workers who manufacture, instal and transport transmission systems, the company said.</p>
<p>About 350 new employees would be hired in development, marketing and product management, it said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
